e gene transfer element derived from <italic>Vibrio cholerae</italic>.</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><volume>184</volume><fpage>4259</fpage><lpage>4269</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12107144</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000439-Hochhut2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hochhut</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldor</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Site-specific integration of the conjugal <italic>Vibrio cholerae</italic> SXT element into <italic>prfC</italic>.</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><volume>32</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10216863</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000439-Burrus3"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burrus</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldor</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Control of SXT integration and excision.</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><volume>185</volume><fpage>5045</fpage><lpage>5054</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12923077</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000439-Beaber3"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beaber</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldor</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Identification of operators and promoters that control SXT conjugative transfer.</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><volume>186</volume><fpage>5945</fpage><lpage>5949</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15317801</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000439-Beaber4"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surn